---
import GuideLayout from "../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
import SourceBadge from "../../components/SourceBadge.astro";
import InfoCard from "../../components/InfoCard.astro";

const LAST_CHECKED = "2026-08-22";

const toc = [
	{ href: "#overview", label: "Overview" },
	{ href: "#advancement", label: "How to advance" },
	{ href: "#ap", label: "AP allocation" },
	{ href: "#skills", label: "First job skills" },
	{ href: "#training", label: "Training routes" },
	{ href: "#equipment", label: "Equipment" },
	{ href: "#second-job", label: "Second job branches" },
	{ href: "#faq", label: "FAQ" },
];

// Every content block on this page comes from v83 baseline knowledge
// and needs Classic World verification. The SourceCard footer already
// makes this clear; the per-section VerificationNotices reinforce it.
const guideSources = [
	"ayumilove-v83-warrior",
	"hiddenstreet-v83-database",
];

// First-job skills structured as data so the table renders cleanly
// and future MDX migration is trivial (this becomes frontmatter).
const firstJobSkills = [
	{
		name: "Improved Max HP Recovery",
		type: "Passive",
		maxLevel: "16 (v83)",
		summary: "Faster natural HP regeneration over time.",
		suggested: "1 point (prerequisite for other passives)",
	},
	{
		name: "Improved Max HP Increase",
		type: "Passive",
		maxLevel: "10 (v83)",
		summary: "Bonus HP gained per level-up. Compounds with every level, so investing early pays for the rest of the character's life.",
		suggested: "Max out first (v83 baseline)",
	},
	{
		name: "Iron Body",
		type: "Buff",
		maxLevel: "20 (v83)",
		summary: "Temporary boost to Weapon Defense.",
		suggested: "Skip early or 1-point utility; damage skills come first",
	},
	{
		name: "Power Strike",
		type: "Attack",
		maxLevel: "20 (v83)",
		summary: "Single strong hit. Higher damage-per-point than Slash Blast against single targets.",
		suggested: "Max after HP passive (v83 baseline)",
	},
	{
		name: "Slash Blast",
		type: "Attack",
		maxLevel: "20 (v83)",
		summary: "Short-range AoE hit. The AoE pick once you start training on grouped mobs.",
		suggested: "Max after Power Strike (v83 baseline)",
	},
];

const secondJobs = [
	{
		name: "Fighter",
		weapon: "Sword or Axe",
		summary: "Highest sustained single-target damage in v83. Party utility via Rage (+ATT buff). Straightforward, damage-first playstyle.",
		bestFor: "Players who want pure DPS and a simple decision tree",
	},
	{
		name: "Page",
		weapon: "Sword or Blunt Weapon (BW)",
		summary: "Utility and control. Threaten debuffs mob attack; strong element-based follow-up skills at 3rd job. Historically the least DPS-focused of the three.",
		bestFor: "Players who value party utility and lower damage-taken over raw output",
	},
	{
		name: "Spearman",
		weapon: "Spear or Polearm",
		summary: "AoE-focused. Iron Will (party Weapon Def buff). Later unlocks Hyper Body (+HP/MP for the party) which is a core group-content buff.",
		bestFor: "Players who plan to party a lot and want to bring buffs everyone loves",
	},
];
---

<GuideLayout
	title="Warrior - Liven's Classic Maple Guide"
	currentPath="/jobs"
	theme="perion"
	decorations={true}
	eyebrow="Class Guide"
	heading="Warrior"
	tagline="High HP, high defense, melee physical damage. The class that survives your mistakes."
	verificationStatus="historical-archive"
	lastChecked={LAST_CHECKED}
	sourceSlugs={guideSources}
	verificationNote="Every claim here reflects v83-era baseline. Classic World values will be re-verified once Founder's Access begins on October 6."
	toc={toc}
>
	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="overview" class="guide-section">
		<h2>Overview</h2>
		<div class="card prose">
			<p>
				Warriors are Classic World's melee tank archetype: high HP,
				high defense, and STR-based physical damage. They trade the
				ranged safety of Bowmen and the magical utility of Magicians
				for the ability to walk into a mob and stay there.
			</p>
			<p>
				The class rewards steady play. Damage scales primarily off
				STR and weapon choice; survival scales off HP investment and
				defensive equipment. There is no mana-management minigame,
				no positional dance - the moment-to-moment gameplay is
				"attack, watch HP, use a potion when needed."
			</p>

			<div class="callout">
				<strong>Best for:</strong> players who want to survive
				mistakes, prefer simple decision trees, or plan to party
				often and appreciate having the meat shield.
				<br />
				<strong>Not ideal for:</strong> players who want ranged
				safety (Bowman), magical burst (Magician), or high-mobility
				assassination gameplay (Thief).
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="advancement" class="guide-section">
		<h2>How to become a Warrior</h2>

		<div class="card prose">
			<p><strong>Requirements (v83 baseline):</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>Character level <strong>10</strong></li>
				<li>At least <strong>35 STR</strong></li>
			</ul>

			<p><strong>Where to go:</strong></p>
			<ol>
				<li>
					From Lith Harbor (arrival point after Maple Island), take
					the taxi or travel to <strong>Perion</strong> in Ossyria.
				</li>
				<li>
					Enter the <em>Chief's Residence</em> in Perion and speak
					with <strong>Dances with Balrog</strong>, the Warrior job
					instructor.
				</li>
				<li>
					Accept the job change. Historically this was a direct
					conversation with no combat trial - Classic World may
					reintroduce an advancement quest. See FAQ below.
				</li>
			</ol>

			<p>
				After advancement you gain 1 SP and unlock the first job
				skill set (listed below).
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="ap" class="guide-section">
		<h2>AP allocation</h2>

		<div class="card prose">
			<p>
				<strong>The short version (v83 baseline):</strong> pour
				points into STR every level. DEX only exists to keep your
				hit rate acceptable.
			</p>

			<p><strong>Two schools of thought exist:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Pure STR:</strong> Every AP into STR. Maximum
					damage output; you will miss more often, especially on
					same-level or higher mobs.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>DEX = (character level - 1):</strong> Keep DEX
					one below your level for reliable hit rate. Slightly
					lower damage; substantially more consistent.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				The DEX-level rule is the more forgiving choice for a first
				character and the recommendation most v83 guides made. Whether
				the hit-rate formula still behaves this way in Classic World
				is one of the values we will verify at launch.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="skills" class="guide-section">
		<h2>First job skills</h2>

		<p class="section-lede">
			First job gives you five skills. The recommended v83 order is:
			<strong>1 point in Improved HP Recovery,</strong> then max
			Improved MaxHP Increase, then max Power Strike, then max Slash
			Blast, then Iron Body with anything left over.
		</p>

		<div class="skill-table" role="table" aria-label="Warrior first job skills">
			<div class="skill-table__header" role="row">
				<span role="columnheader">Skill</span>
				<span role="columnheader">Type</span>
				<span role="columnheader">Summary</span>
				<span role="columnheader">Suggested investment</span>
			</div>
			{firstJobSkills.map((skill) => (
				<div class="skill-table__row" role="row">
					<div role="cell">
						<strong>{skill.name}</strong>
						<small>Max Level: {skill.maxLevel}</small>
					</div>
					<div role="cell">{skill.type}</div>
					<div role="cell">{skill.summary}</div>
					<div role="cell">{skill.suggested}</div>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="training" class="guide-section">
		<h2>Training routes (levels 1-30)</h2>

		<p class="section-lede">
			v83 baseline routes. Classic World map spawns and monster
			levels may have shifted; verify at Founder's Access.
		</p>

		<div class="route-grid">
			<div class="card route-card">
				<h3>Levels 1 - 10 (Beginner)</h3>
				<p><strong>Where:</strong> Maple Island</p>
				<p><strong>What:</strong> Snails, Blue Snails, Red Snails</p>
				<p>Complete the Maple Island story quests, then take the ship to Victoria Island. Reach 35 STR before hitting Perion.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="card route-card">
				<h3>Levels 10 - 15</h3>
				<p><strong>Where:</strong> Henesys area or Perion outskirts</p>
				<p><strong>What:</strong> Orange Mushrooms, Green Snails, Ribbon Pigs</p>
				<p>Get comfortable with Power Strike here. Party quests are usually low priority at this range.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="card route-card">
				<h3>Levels 15 - 25</h3>
				<p><strong>Where:</strong> Perion (Stumps, Axe Stumps), Kerning City (Ligators, Octopus), or Ellinia (Green Trixters)</p>
				<p><strong>What:</strong> Whichever has fewer players competing for spawns.</p>
				<p>This is where Slash Blast starts pulling ahead if you find grouped mobs.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="card route-card">
				<h3>Levels 25 - 30</h3>
				<p><strong>Where:</strong> Perion Excavation Site (Fire Boars) or Ant Tunnel entrance (Zombie Mushrooms)</p>
				<p><strong>What:</strong> Denser mobs, higher EXP-per-kill.</p>
				<p>Second job advancement quest becomes available at level 30. Save some mesos for the second-job weapon.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="equipment" class="guide-section">
		<h2>Equipment progression</h2>

		<div class="card prose">
			<p>
				Warrior gear is the least specialized of the four classes:
				you want raw Weapon ATT on your weapon, and Weapon Def with
				STR/DEX bonuses on everything else.
			</p>

			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Level 1 - 10:</strong> Whatever the beginner
					shops sell. Warriors can use most weapon categories, so
					pick whichever your starting mesos allow.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Level 10 - 20:</strong> A basic sword or axe
					from Perion's weapon shop. Look for drops from Stumps.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Level 20 - 30:</strong> Zombie's Lost Gold Tooth
					(sword) or a Fusion Axe were common v83 upgrades. Check
					the market before hunting - drops can be cheaper than
					farm time.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Approaching 30:</strong> Save mesos for the
					second-job weapon you have already chosen. Second-job
					weapons are a large power jump.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="callout">
				<strong>Scroll safely.</strong> Ten-percent scrolls with
				stat boosts read tempting but usually destroy your gear at
				this level range. Sixty and hundred-percent scrolls are the
				beginner-friendly choices.
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="second-job" class="guide-section">
		<h2>Second job branches (level 30)</h2>

		<p class="section-lede">
			At level 30 you choose one of three second-job paths. All are
			viable; the pick shapes what you do for the next 40+ levels.
		</p>

		<div class="branches-grid">
			{secondJobs.map((job) => (
				<article class="card branch-card">
					<h3>{job.name}</h3>
					<p class="branch-card__weapon">
						<strong>Weapon:</strong> {job.weapon}
					</p>
					<p>{job.summary}</p>
					<p class="branch-card__for">
						<strong>Best for:</strong> {job.bestFor}
					</p>
				</article>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ============================================================ -->
	<section id="faq" class="guide-section">
		<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

		<InfoCard eyebrow="FAQ" heading="Common Warrior questions">
			<dl class="faq">
				<dt>Do I need to do a job advancement quest, or just talk?</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>Awaiting confirmation.</em> v83 was talk-only; some
					later versions added a "prove yourself" combat trial.
					Which one Classic World uses will be visible at Founder's
					Access.
					<span class="inline-badge"><SourceBadge type="awaiting-confirmation" compact /></span>
				</dd>

				<dt>Is pure STR still viable at launch?</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>Awaiting confirmation.</em> Depends on the hit-rate
					formula. In v83 pure STR was playable but painful. If
					Classic World keeps the same math, DEX = (level - 1)
					stays the safer general recommendation.
					<span class="inline-badge"><SourceBadge type="awaiting-confirmation" compact /></span>
				</dd>

				<dt>Which second job does the most damage?</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>v83 baseline:</em> Fighter had the highest sustained
					single-target output; Spearman won on AoE; Page had the
					best party utility but the lowest raw DPS. Classic World
					may rebalance any of these.
					<span class="inline-badge"><SourceBadge type="historical-archive" compact /></span>
				</dd>

				<dt>Can I change my mind at second job?</dt>
				<dd>
					No. Second job is a one-time choice per character. If
					you want to try another branch, you make a new Warrior.
				</dd>

				<dt>Do I need to grind Mark of Beta on this character?</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>Awaiting confirmation.</em> Mark of Beta details are
					not public yet. If it is per-character rather than
					per-account, it will affect early-game choices - see the
					<a href="/launch#mark-of-beta">Launch Hub Mark of Beta
					section</a>.
					<span class="inline-badge"><SourceBadge type="awaiting-confirmation" compact /></span>
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</InfoCard>
	</section>
</GuideLayout>

{/* Guide section styles (.guide-section, .prose, .callout, .skill-table,
	.route-grid, .branches-grid, .faq, .inline-badge) live in global.css
	so every job guide inherits them without duplicating ~120 lines of CSS. */}
